/-!
# An invertible module on a quasi-affine Noetherian scheme is the sheaf of a divisor

Let `X` be a Noetherian scheme and `𝒩` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module. The slogan behind
[Stacks, Tag 0AYM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AYM) is that `𝒩` has a *regular
meromorphic section*: a global section of `𝒩` whose vanishing locus is an honest divisor rather
than a component of `X`. The obstruction is that a global section of `𝒩` may vanish on a whole
irreducible component, and the whole point is to choose it so that it does not: it suffices that
it be nonvanishing at each of the finitely many associated points of `X`
([Stacks, Tag 05AF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AF)), for then it is a regular section
([Stacks, Tag 0AYL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AYL)) and its zero scheme is an
effective Cartier divisor `D` with `𝒩 ≅ 𝒪_X(D)`
([Stacks, Tag 01X0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01X0)).

On a **quasi-affine** `X` such a section exists outright, because an invertible module on a
quasi-affine scheme has a global section nonvanishing at any prescribed finite set of points
([Stacks, Tag 0F20](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F20)). Feeding the associated points
together with a prescribed finite set `E` into that statement gives the quasi-affine clause of
Tag 0AYM, which is what this file proves. Its vanishing locus misses `E` because `E` lies in the
nonvanishing open.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_invertibleSheaf_of_isQuasiAffine`:
  **the quasi-affine clause of [Stacks, Tag 0AYM]**. On a Noetherian quasi-affine scheme every
  invertible module is `𝒪_X(D)` for an effective Cartier divisor `D` disjoint from any
  prescribed finite subset — the case `D' = ∅` of the general statement.

## Implementation notes

A divisor is carried by its quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals, `Scheme.IdealSheafData`, and its
underlying closed set is `Scheme.IdealSheafData.supportSet`; `𝒪_X(D)` is
`Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf'`. The isomorphism `𝒩 ≅ 𝒪_X(D)` is produced as data inside a
`Nonempty`, since the statement asserts only that one exists — Tag 01X0 pins down a unique one
matching the canonical section of `𝒪_X(D)` with the chosen section of `𝒩`, and that uniqueness
is not part of Tag 0AYM.

Disjointness from `E` is deduced from the stronger fact that the *whole* nonvanishing open of
the chosen section misses the support of the divisor. That is checked on an affine open `V`
inside the nonvanishing open, where the section trivializes the module: the defining ideal of
the zero scheme is generated by the function representing the section
(`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization`), which is here the unit, so the ideal is
the whole ring and the zero locus of `V` is empty.

The general clause of Tag 0AYM — a difference `𝒪_X(D - D')` for `X` carrying an ample invertible
sheaf — is *not* proved here. Its proof picks `s ∈ Γ(X, ℒ^{⊗ m})` with `X_s` affine and containing
the finite set ([Stacks, Tag 09NV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09NV)), uses the
quasi-affine case on `X_s` to get a section of `𝒩` there, and extends it to a global section of
`𝒩 ⊗ ℒ^{⊗ p}` by [Stacks, Tag 01PW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PW); both that global
section and the corresponding power of `s` are then regular, giving `D` and `D'`. The extension
step is available as
`Stacks.ModuleSectionExtension.exists_tensorPow_tensorSection_of_isAmple`, and the nonvanishing of
the extended section follows from
`Stacks.TensorSectionProduct.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff_of_resTop_eq`. What is missing is the
middle step: `Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus` is defined for *global* sections only, so a section
of `𝒩` over `X_s` produced on `X_s.toScheme` has no nonvanishing locus in `X` to compare with —
the comparison recorded as outstanding in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/AmplePullbackPart1/Restriction.lean` and in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/PullbackExtension/Basic.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AYM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AYM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AYL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AYL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01X0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01X0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F20](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F20)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AF)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A global section `s` of an invertible module `𝒩` on a locally Noetherian scheme which is
nonvanishing at every associated point of `X` cuts out an effective Cartier divisor `D` with
`𝒩 ≅ 𝒪_X(D)`, and the support of `D` is disjoint from every subset of the nonvanishing locus
of `s`. -/
theorem exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_of_nonvanishing
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (N : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (s : N.sections) {E : Set X}
    (hE : E ⊆ Stacks.NonvanishingTrivialize.nonvanishingLocus X.toRingedSpace N s)
    (hAss : Stacks.Divisors.schemeAssociatedPoints X ⊆
      Stacks.NonvanishingTrivialize.nonvanishingLocus X.toRingedSpace N s) :
    ∃ D : X.IdealSheafData,
      Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D ∧
      Disjoint E D.supportSet ∧
      Nonempty (N ≅ Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf' D) := by
  classical
  have hsregular : IsRegularSection X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property s :=
    (Stacks.Divisors.isRegularSection_iff_forall_associatedPoint_notMem_maximalSmul N s).2
      fun x hx => hAss hx
  set O : X.Opens := Stacks.NonvanishingTrivialize.nonvanishingOpen X.toRingedSpace N s
  set D : X.IdealSheafData := zeroScheme X N (s.eval (op ⊤)) with hDdef
  have hD : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D :=
    (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_iff_isRegularSection X N s).2 hsregular
  obtain ⟨e, -⟩ := (existsUnique_invertibleSheafIso_zeroScheme X N s hsregular).exists
  have hzeroOpen : Disjoint (O : Set X) D.supportSet := by
    rw [Set.disjoint_left]
    intro x hxO hxD
    obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, hVO⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens) hxO
    let U : X.affineOpens := ⟨V, hV⟩
    have hxU : x ∈ (U : X.Opens) := hxV
    let _ : Module Γ(X, U.1) (N.val.obj (op U.1)) := (N.val.obj (op U.1)).isModule
    let f := (N.unitHomEquiv.symm s).over O
    let _ : IsIso f := Stacks.NonvanishingTrivialize.isIso_over_nonvanishingOpen s
    -- `s` is a basis of `𝒩` over `V`, so it is represented by the unit function there
    let fΓ : Γ(X, U.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(N, U.1) :=
      ((SheafOfModules.evaluation (X.ringCatSheaf.over O)
        (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hVO)))).mapIso (asIso f)).toLinearEquiv
    have hsection :
        fΓ.symm (N.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op (s.eval (op ⊤))) = (1 : Γ(X, U.1)) := by
      have hfsection :
          fΓ (1 : Γ(X, U.1)) = N.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op (s.eval (op ⊤)) := by
        change ((N.unitHomEquiv.symm s).val.app (op U.1)).hom (1 : Γ(X, U.1)) = _
        rw [Scheme.Modules.unitHomEquiv_symm_app_apply, one_smul]
      rw [← hfsection, fΓ.symm_apply_apply]
    have hideal : D.ideal U = ⊤ := by
      rw [hDdef, zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization X N (s.eval (op ⊤)) U fΓ.symm 1 hsection]
      simp
    have hxzero : x ∈ X.zeroLocus (U := U.1) (↑(D.ideal U)) :=
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_of_mem (I := D) (U := U) hxU).mp hxD
    rw [hideal] at hxzero
    exact (by simpa using hxzero : x ∉ (U : Set X)) hxU
  exact ⟨D, hD, Set.disjoint_of_subset_left (fun x hx => hE hx) hzeroOpen, ⟨e.symm⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AYM**, the quasi-affine clause. On a Noetherian quasi-affine scheme
every invertible `𝒪_X`-module `𝒩` is isomorphic to the invertible sheaf `𝒪_X(D)` of an effective
Cartier divisor `D`, and `D` may be chosen disjoint from any prescribed finite subset `E` of `X`.
This is the case `D' = ∅` of the general statement `𝒩 ≅ 𝒪_X(D - D')`. -/
@[stacks 0AYM "quasi-affine case with empty negative divisor"]
theorem exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_invertibleSheaf_of_isQuasiAffine
    [IsNoetherian X] [X.IsQuasiAffine] (N : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    {E : Set X} (hE : E.Finite) :
    ∃ D : X.IdealSheafData,
      Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D ∧
      Disjoint E D.supportSet ∧
      Nonempty (N ≅ Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf' D) := by
  classical
  have hassoc : (Stacks.Divisors.schemeAssociatedPoints X).Finite := by
    have h := associatedPoints_inter_finite (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) ⊤
      (by simpa using (isCompact_univ : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set X)))
    simpa [Stacks.Divisors.schemeAssociatedPoints] using h
  have : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X N := ‹_›
  obtain ⟨s, -, hTnonzero, -⟩ :=
    Stacks.QuasiAffineGlobalGeneration.exists_affine_nonvanishingOpen_containing_finite_sections
      N (hE.union hassoc) ⊤ (fun x _ => trivial)
  exact exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_of_nonvanishing N s
    (fun _ hx => hTnonzero (Or.inl hx)) (fun _ hx => hTnonzero (Or.inr hx))

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
